      <link>https://www.hercampus.com/school/texas/ancestry-under-surveillance-what-ice-is-taking-from-us/</link>
      <description>This is one of the quieter violences of ICE. Beyond raids, detentions, and deportations, its presence reshapes how people relate to their own identities. It teaches us to second-guess self-knowledge, to treat heritage as a liability, to see our neighborhoods not as homes but as targets. ICE does not only remove people from their families; it erodes the sense of safety required to ask fundamental human questions: Where do I come from? &amp;lt;p&amp;gt;The post Underlying Liability: What ICE Is Taking from Us f</description>
